### Ledgerly: newer features (deposit/withdraw, payees, insights, notifications, profile, admin)
### Open in VS Code with the REST Client extension and click "Send Request" above each block.
### Run the login request first; later requests reuse its token.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080/api

# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "testuser",
  "password": "Test@1234"
}

###
@token = {{login.response.body.token}}

### Open an account with an opening deposit (recorded as a DEPOSIT transaction)
# @name acc
POST {{baseUrl}}/accounts
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "accountType": "SAVINGS",
  "nickname": "Everyday",
  "openingDeposit": 25000
}

###
@acc = {{acc.response.body.accountNumber}}

### Deposit
POST {{baseUrl}}/transactions/deposit
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "accountNumber": "{{acc}}", "amount": 5000, "category": "SALARY", "description": "Salary" }

### Withdraw
POST {{baseUrl}}/transactions/withdraw
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "accountNumber": "{{acc}}", "amount": 1000 }

### Look up who owns an account number before paying (name is partly hidden)
GET {{baseUrl}}/accounts/lookup/{{acc}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Account history with running balance
GET {{baseUrl}}/transactions/account/{{acc}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Search / filter all my transactions (every parameter is optional)
GET {{baseUrl}}/transactions/my?direction=DEBIT&category=FOOD&from=2026-01-01&q=dinner
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### CSV statement
GET {{baseUrl}}/transactions/account/{{acc}}/statement?from=2026-01-01
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Saved payees
GET {{baseUrl}}/beneficiaries
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Add a payee (use someone else's account number)
POST {{baseUrl}}/beneficiaries
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "accountNumber": "ACC0000000000000", "nickname": "Landlord" }

### Insights (monthly in/out, spending by category, top payees)
GET {{baseUrl}}/insights
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Notifications
GET {{baseUrl}}/notifications
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Mark all notifications read
POST {{baseUrl}}/notifications/read-all
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### My profile
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Change password
PUT {{baseUrl}}/users/me/password
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "currentPassword": "Test@1234", "newPassword": "New@12345" }

### Close an account (balance must be 0)
POST {{baseUrl}}/accounts/{{acc}}/close
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ======================= ADMIN =======================
### Start the backend with ADMIN_PASSWORD set to create the admin user.

# @name admin
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "admin", "password": "Admin@12345" }

###
@adminToken = {{admin.response.body.token}}

### Bank-wide stats
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/stats
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### All customers
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/users
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### Freeze an account
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/admin/accounts/{{acc}}/freeze
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "frozen": true }

### Deactivate a customer (use an id from /admin/users)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/admin/users/2/status
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "active": false }
